{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.QHookProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QHookProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HookLengthFormula","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.wedderburn_trace_identity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct_one_mul_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct_one_mul_num","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookProduct.lean#L58-L67","doc":"**The classical HLF is the `q = 1` specialization of the q-hook identity.** The general-`n`\nq-hook product at `q = 1`, times the genuine standard-tableau count `#SYT(μ)`, equals\n`[n]_q!|_{q=1} = n!` — i.e. the machine-checked classical Frame–Robinson–Thrall HLF\n(`numStandardYoungTableaux_mul_hookLengthProduct`, #4041) *is* the `q → 1` limit of the\nq-hook identity `dim_q(μ)·∏[hook]_q = [n]_q!`. Over any `[Field R]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.qFactorial_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.qFactorial_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookProduct.lean#L49-L56","doc":"**q-factorial at `q = 1` = `n!`** (cast to `R`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct_one","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookProduct.lean#L42-L47","doc":"**q-hook product at `q = 1` = classical hook product** (cast to `R`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.qIntGeo_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.qIntGeo_one","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookProduct.lean#L37-L40","doc":"The Gaussian q-integer at `q = 1` is the plain integer: `[k]_1 = k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.qHookLengthProduct","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookProduct.lean#L32-L35","doc":"**The q-hook product** `∏_{c∈μ} [hook(c)]_q` — q-analogue of `hookLengthProduct`, over the\ncorpus Gaussian q-integer `[k]_q = ∑_{i<k} q^i` (`QOU.BraidKnot.qIntGeo`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}